# No push or deploy without full mobile proof

## Policy

**Do not push, deploy, or declare the app ready** until the entire vault app is tested on real mobile (375×812, JS enabled) — not just Recruiting hero, not just the menu, not SSR-only screenshots.

## Required proof package

Run after local `npm run build:netlify` merge:

```bash
npm run proof:mobile:deploy
```

Output: `proof/mobile-deploy-proof/`

### Screenshots (every route)

- `/vault/`
- `/vault/recruiting/`
- `/vault/team/`
- `/vault/futurecast/`
- `/vault/schedule/`
- `/vault/film-room/` (user path: `/vault/film/`)
- `/vault/articles/`
- `/vault/nil/`
- `/vault/live/podcasts/` (user path: `/vault/podcasts/`)
- `/vault/tickets/`

Plus **menu open + menu closed** screenshot on each route.

### Screen recordings (cold load)

- `/vault/` loading (~15s)
- `/vault/recruiting/` loading (~15s)
- `/vault/team/` loading (~18s)

### Section checklist (pass/fail)

| Section | Where |
|---------|-------|
| Roster | Team hub |
| Depth chart | Team hub |
| Staff | Team staff room (`/vault/team/staff/`) |
| Pipeline | Recruiting footprint map |
| Movement | Recruiting (2028 open-cycle shell) |
| Beat intel | Home |
| GNL | Live feed |
| FutureCast | FutureCast page |
| Class cards | Recruiting hero year tabs |
| Everything below NSD | Movement, battle board, footprint, position snapshot (2028 for war-room stack) |

All rows must **PASS** in `CHECKLIST.md` and `checklist.json`.

### Automated verification

`proof:mobile:deploy` also runs **3 consecutive passes** of `verify:mobile:full`.

### After Netlify deploy

```bash
npm run verify:netlify:build
```

Confirms:

1. Latest Netlify deploy state is `ready` (when `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` + `NETLIFY_SITE_ID` set)
2. Production `gatorvault-build` meta matches local `server/build-manifest.json` commit

## Blockers

- Any checklist FAIL
- Menu fails to open/close on any route
- Blank pages, eternal skeletons, "Loading roster…", React #423
- Production build ID does not match commit

## Workflow

1. Fix failures locally until `npm run proof:mobile:deploy` passes
2. Push only when user explicitly requests
3. After Netlify build completes: `npm run verify:netlify:build`
4. Share `proof/mobile-deploy-proof/` with user before claiming deploy success
